IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `act-nouns`
IMPORT `act-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `act-ch13-structure`

-- Tests for act-ch13-structure.l4.
-- Every expected value is read from the section named beside the assertion, and was written before the run.

§ `Tests: chapter 13, Structure of Acts and statutory instruments`

§§ `Part 13.1: General`

-- s 125: law means an Act, subordinate law or disallowable instrument.
#ASSERT `s 125: the kind of document is a law for chapter 13` `an Act`
#ASSERT `s 125: the kind of document is a law for chapter 13` `a subordinate law`
#ASSERT `s 125: the kind of document is a law for chapter 13` `a disallowable instrument`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 125: the kind of document is a law for chapter 13` `a notifiable instrument`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 125: the kind of document is a law for chapter 13` `a commencement notice`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 125: the kind of document is a law for chapter 13` `a statutory instrument of another kind`)

-- s 126 (1): a heading to a chapter, part, division, subdivision, schedule or another provision (other than a section or subsection) is part of the Act or instrument.
#ASSERT `s 126, s 127: the material is part of the Act or instrument` `a heading to a chapter, part, division, subdivision, schedule, or another provision (other than a section or subsection)` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 126 (2) and s 127 (3): a heading to a section or subsection is part of the Act if s 126 (2) applies, and is not part of it if s 126 (2) does not apply.
#ASSERT `s 126, s 127: the material is part of the Act or instrument` `a heading to a section or subsection` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 126, s 127: the material is part of the Act or instrument` `a heading to a section or subsection` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 126 (3) to (7): a preamble or recital; an example or diagram; a schedule, dictionary or appendix; punctuation; a provision number: each is part of the Act or instrument.
#ASSERT `s 126, s 127: the material is part of the Act or instrument` `a preamble or other recital` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 126, s 127: the material is part of the Act or instrument` `an example or diagram` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 126, s 127: the material is part of the Act or instrument` `a schedule, dictionary or appendix` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 126, s 127: the material is part of the Act or instrument` `punctuation` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 126, s 127: the material is part of the Act or instrument` `a provision number` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 127 (1), (2): a footnote, endnote or other note; a table of contents, reader's guide or index: each is not part of the Act or instrument.
#ASSERT `s 126, s 127: the material is part of the Act or instrument` `a footnote, endnote or other note` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 126, s 127: the material is part of the Act or instrument` `a table of contents, reader's guide or index` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Material neither section names.
#ASSERT `s 126, s 127: the material is part of the Act or instrument` `material of some other kind` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 126 (8), s 127 (6): for an Act or instrument divided otherwise than into sections, a reference to a section or subsection is a reference to a corresponding provision.
#ASSERT `s 126 (8), s 127 (6): a reference to a section or subsection is a reference to a corresponding provision` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 126 (8), s 127 (6): a reference to a section or subsection is a reference to a corresponding provision` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 127 (4): this section does not prevent the amendment of a note, table, guide, index or heading.
#ASSERT NOT `s 127 (4): this section prevents the amendment of a note, table, guide, index or heading`
-- s 127 (5): such a note, table, guide or index does not become part of the Act or instrument because it is amended or inserted.
#ASSERT `s 127 (5): the note, table, guide or index becomes part of the Act or instrument because it is amended or inserted` `a footnote, endnote or other note` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 127 (5): the note, table, guide or index becomes part of the Act or instrument because it is amended or inserted` `a table of contents, reader's guide or index` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 127 (5): the note, table, guide or index becomes part of the Act or instrument because it is amended or inserted` `a footnote, endnote or other note` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 127 (5): the note, table, guide or index becomes part of the Act or instrument because it is amended or inserted` `a heading to a section or subsection` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Part 13.2: Particular kinds of provisions`

-- s 130: a definition is a provision (however expressed) of an Act or statutory instrument that gives a meaning to a term, or limits or extends its meaning.
-- s 130 Example 1: "X means Y."
#ASSERT `s 130: the provision is a definition` TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- s 130 Example 2: "X includes Y." (extends the meaning)
#ASSERT `s 130: the provision is a definition` TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- s 130 Example 3: "X means Y, and includes Z."
#ASSERT `s 130: the provision is a definition` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- s 130 Example 4: "A reference to X is a reference to Y."
#ASSERT `s 130: the provision is a definition` TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- s 130 Example 5: "X—see section Y." (a signpost definition)
#ASSERT `s 130: the provision is a definition` TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- s 130 Example 6: "X—see the XYZ Act 1999, section Y."
#ASSERT `s 130: the provision is a definition` TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- s 130 Example 7: "In a proceeding against a person (the retailer), it is a defence if the retailer establishes that the goods were bought honestly." (a tagged term)
#ASSERT `s 130: the provision is a definition` TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- s 130 Example 8: "excluded—a claim is excluded if the claim is not brought within 1 year ..." (does not begin with the defined term)
#ASSERT `s 130: the provision is a definition` TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- s 130 Example 9: "A term used in the XYZ Act 2003 has the same meaning in this Act."
#ASSERT `s 130: the provision is a definition` TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- s 130 Example 10: "A term defined in the XYZ Act 2003 has the same meaning in this Act."
#ASSERT `s 130: the provision is a definition` TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- A provision that neither gives, limits nor extends a meaning, and a provision of something other than an Act or statutory instrument, are not definitions.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 130: the provision is a definition` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 130: the provision is a definition` FALSE TRUE TRUE)

-- s 131 (1) Example 1: 'food—see section 10.' gives the word 'food' the meaning it has in section 10.
#ASSERT `s 131 (1): the meaning a signpost definition gives the term` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the meaning the term itself has in the law or instrument referred to`
-- s 131 (1) Example 2: 'injury—see the XYZ Act 2001, dictionary.' gives the word 'injury' the meaning it has in the definition of injury in that dictionary.
#ASSERT `s 131 (1): the meaning a signpost definition gives the term` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the meaning the term itself has in the law or instrument referred to`
-- s 131 (1) Example 3: 'Work Safety Council—see the XYZ Act 2000, dictionary, definition of council.' gives the expression the meaning of 'council' in that dictionary.
#ASSERT `s 131 (1): the meaning a signpost definition gives the term` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the meaning the other term named in the reference has in the law or instrument referred to`
-- A definition without 'see' followed by a reference to a law or instrument is not a signpost definition.
#ASSERT `s 131 (1): the meaning a signpost definition gives the term` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 131 (1): the meaning a signpost definition gives the term` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 131 (2): this section is subject to section 47.
#ASSERT `s 131 (2): the sections that s 131 is subject to` EQUALS LIST "47"

-- s 132 (1): an example is not exhaustive; it may extend, but does not limit, the meaning.
#ASSERT NOT `s 132 (1) (a): an example is exhaustive`
#ASSERT `s 132 (1) (b): an example may extend the meaning of the Act or instrument, or of the provision to which it relates`
#ASSERT NOT `s 132 (1) (b): an example limits the meaning of the Act or instrument, or of the provision to which it relates`
-- s 132 (2) (a): a statement at the end of the provision it illustrates (or of a provision containing it); (b): a statement forming part of the text of a provision that illustrates its operation.
#ASSERT `s 132 (2): the statement has a form an example may take` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 132 (2): the statement has a form an example may take` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 132 (2): the statement has a form an example may take` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 132 (2): the statement has a form an example may take` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 132 (3): subsection (2) does not limit the form that an example may take.
#ASSERT NOT `s 132 (3): subsection (2) limits the form that an example may take`

§§ `Section 133`

-- s 133 (1): in a law, a penalty expressed as a number (whole or fractional) of penalty units is a fine of that number of penalty units.
#ASSERT `s 133 (1): the fine, in penalty units` `an Act` TRUE 20 EQUALS JUST 20
#ASSERT `s 133 (1): the fine, in penalty units` `a subordinate law` TRUE 0.5 EQUALS JUST 0.5
#ASSERT `s 133 (1): the fine, in penalty units` `a disallowable instrument` TRUE 100 EQUALS JUST 100
#ASSERT `s 133 (1): the fine, in penalty units` `an Act` FALSE 20 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 133 (1): the fine, in penalty units` `a notifiable instrument` TRUE 20 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 133 (2): a penalty unit is $160 for an offence committed by an individual, $810 for a corporation.
#ASSERT `s 133 (2): the amount of a penalty unit, in dollars` `an individual` EQUALS JUST 160
#ASSERT `s 133 (2): the amount of a penalty unit, in dollars` `a corporation` EQUALS JUST 810
#ASSERT `s 133 (2): the amount of a penalty unit, in dollars` `an offender who is neither an individual nor a corporation` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 133 (1) and (2) together.
#ASSERT `s 133 (1), (2): the fine, in dollars` `an Act` `an individual` TRUE 20 EQUALS JUST 3200
#ASSERT `s 133 (1), (2): the fine, in dollars` `an Act` `a corporation` TRUE 20 EQUALS JUST 16200
#ASSERT `s 133 (1), (2): the fine, in dollars` `a subordinate law` `an individual` TRUE 1.5 EQUALS JUST 240
#ASSERT `s 133 (1), (2): the fine, in dollars` `a subordinate law` `a corporation` TRUE 0.5 EQUALS JUST 405
#ASSERT `s 133 (1), (2): the fine, in dollars` `an Act` `an individual` FALSE 20 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 133 (1), (2): the fine, in dollars` `an Act` `an offender who is neither an individual nor a corporation` TRUE 20 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 133 (3): review at least once every 4 years after the day the subsection commences.
-- A day that is the 31st of December begins a run of 4 calendar years on the next day.
#ASSERT `s 133 (3): the last day by which the Attorney-General must have reviewed the amount of a penalty unit` (Date 31 12 2019) 1 EQUALS JUST (Date 31 12 2023)
#ASSERT `s 133 (3): the last day by which the Attorney-General must have reviewed the amount of a penalty unit` (Date 31 12 2019) 2 EQUALS JUST (Date 31 12 2027)
-- A start in the middle of a year: the text gives no rule for years that do not begin on 1 January, so the answer is NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 133 (3): the last day by which the Attorney-General must have reviewed the amount of a penalty unit` (Date 16 7 2025) 1 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Sections 134 and 135`

-- s 134 (1) (a), (b) and s 135 (1): which section governs a stated penalty.
#ASSERT `s 134 (1), s 135 (1): the section that governs the stated penalty` `at the end of a section` EQUALS `section 134 governs the penalty`
#ASSERT `s 134 (1), s 135 (1): the section that governs the stated penalty` `at the end of a subsection but not at the end of a section` EQUALS `section 134 governs the penalty`
#ASSERT `s 134 (1), s 135 (1): the section that governs the stated penalty` `in a provision, other than at the end of a section or subsection` EQUALS `section 135 governs the penalty`

-- s 134 (1) Example, par (a): the penalty 'Maximum penalty: 20 penalty units.' at the end of a section.
#ASSERT `s 134 (1) to (3), s 135 (3): what the stated penalty applies to` `at the end of a section` FALSE EQUALS `the whole section`
-- s 134 (1) Example, par (b): the same penalty at the end of a subsection, but not at the end of a section.
#ASSERT `s 134 (1) to (3), s 135 (3): what the stated penalty applies to` `at the end of a subsection but not at the end of a section` FALSE EQUALS `the whole subsection`
-- s 134 (1) Examples, par (c) 1: 'Maximum penalty (subsection (3)): 20 penalty units.' at the end of a section divided into subsections.
#ASSERT `s 134 (1) to (3), s 135 (3): what the stated penalty applies to` `at the end of a section` TRUE EQUALS `only the relevant provision of the section or subsection`
-- s 134 (1) Examples, par (c) 2: a penalty with 'for paragraph (b)' and 'for another paragraph' at the end of a subsection.
#ASSERT `s 134 (1) to (3), s 135 (3): what the stated penalty applies to` `at the end of a subsection but not at the end of a section` TRUE EQUALS `only the relevant provision of the section or subsection`
-- s 135 (3): a penalty not at the end of a section or subsection is about the provision (or a stated part of it).
#ASSERT `s 134 (1) to (3), s 135 (3): what the stated penalty applies to` `in a provision, other than at the end of a section or subsection` FALSE EQUALS `the provision in which the penalty is stated, or a stated part of it`

-- s 134 (2) Example, penalty applying to entire section or subsection: 'A person must not contravene a notice. Maximum penalty: 20 penalty units.' (no offence mentioned)
#ASSERT `s 134 (2), (3), s 135 (2), (3): what the stated penalty indicates` FALSE EQUALS `contravention is an offence punishable on conviction as subsection (4) provides`
-- s 134 (2) Example, penalty applying to a stated provision: 'Maximum penalty (paragraph (b)): 20 penalty units.' after '(b) must contain the particulars ...' (no offence mentioned)
#ASSERT `s 134 (1) to (3), s 135 (3): what the stated penalty applies to` `at the end of a subsection but not at the end of a section` TRUE EQUALS `only the relevant provision of the section or subsection`
#ASSERT `s 134 (2), (3), s 135 (2), (3): what the stated penalty indicates` FALSE EQUALS `contravention is an offence punishable on conviction as subsection (4) provides`
-- s 134 (3) Example, penalty applying to entire section or subsection: 'A person who contravenes a notice commits an offence. Maximum penalty: 20 penalty units.'
#ASSERT `s 134 (2), (3), s 135 (2), (3): what the stated penalty indicates` TRUE EQUALS `the offence is punishable on conviction as subsection (4) provides`
-- s 134 (3) Example, penalty applying to a stated provision: '(a) the person commits an offence' with 'Maximum penalty (paragraph (a)): 20 penalty units.'
#ASSERT `s 134 (1) to (3), s 135 (3): what the stated penalty applies to` `at the end of a subsection but not at the end of a section` TRUE EQUALS `only the relevant provision of the section or subsection`
#ASSERT `s 134 (2), (3), s 135 (2), (3): what the stated penalty indicates` TRUE EQUALS `the offence is punishable on conviction as subsection (4) provides`
-- s 135 (2) Example: 'A person who contravenes s (3) commits an offence punishable by a fine of not more than 20 penalty units.'
#ASSERT `s 134 (1), s 135 (1): the section that governs the stated penalty` `in a provision, other than at the end of a section or subsection` EQUALS `section 135 governs the penalty`
#ASSERT `s 134 (2), (3), s 135 (2), (3): what the stated penalty indicates` TRUE EQUALS `the offence is punishable on conviction as subsection (4) provides`
-- s 135 (3) Example: 'A person who contravenes s (3) must pay a fine of not more than 20 penalty units.' (no offence mentioned)
#ASSERT `s 134 (2), (3), s 135 (2), (3): what the stated penalty indicates` FALSE EQUALS `contravention is an offence punishable on conviction as subsection (4) provides`

-- s 134 (4) (a), s 135 (4) (a): if only a single penalty is stated, not more than the stated penalty.
#ASSERT `s 134 (4), s 135 (4): the penalty may be imposed` 20 NOTHING 20
#ASSERT `s 134 (4), s 135 (4): the penalty may be imposed` 20 NOTHING 0
#ASSERT NOT (`s 134 (4), s 135 (4): the penalty may be imposed` 20 NOTHING 21)
-- s 134 (4) (b), s 135 (4) (b): if a minimum as well as a maximum is stated, not less than the minimum and not more than the maximum.
#ASSERT `s 134 (4), s 135 (4): the penalty may be imposed` 20 (JUST 10) 10
#ASSERT `s 134 (4), s 135 (4): the penalty may be imposed` 20 (JUST 10) 15
#ASSERT `s 134 (4), s 135 (4): the penalty may be imposed` 20 (JUST 10) 20
#ASSERT NOT (`s 134 (4), s 135 (4): the penalty may be imposed` 20 (JUST 10) 9)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 134 (4), s 135 (4): the penalty may be imposed` 20 (JUST 10) 21)

-- s 134 (5) Example: the penalty at the end of the section (after subsection (4)) is taken to apply only to subsection (4).
#ASSERT `s 134 (5): the first penalty is taken to be expressed as applying only to the last subsection` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 134 (5): the first penalty is taken to be expressed as applying only to the last subsection` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 134 (5): the first penalty is taken to be expressed as applying only to the last subsection` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 134 (5): the first penalty is taken to be expressed as applying only to the last subsection` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 134 (6), s 135 (5): the position of any example or note is disregarded in working out whether a penalty is at the end.
#ASSERT `s 134 (6), s 135 (5): the penalty is at the end of the section or subsection` EMPTY
#ASSERT `s 134 (6), s 135 (5): the penalty is at the end of the section or subsection` (LIST `an example`)
#ASSERT `s 134 (6), s 135 (5): the penalty is at the end of the section or subsection` (LIST `a note`, `an example`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 134 (6), s 135 (5): the penalty is at the end of the section or subsection` (LIST `other text of the provision`))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 134 (6), s 135 (5): the penalty is at the end of the section or subsection` (LIST `an example`, `other text of the provision`))
